"""xhisper-history: the last dictations, newest first.

Each row has Edit, Copy and, when a text field had the focus as the window
opened, Paste (into that field). Edit fixes a dictation in place; the words
you corrected are learned (xhisper-learn diff) so Whisper and auto-edit spell
them right next time.

Opened by `xhisper --history`, by the History chip on the overlay pill, or by
a double tap of the xhisper-hotkey combo. Reads $XHISPER_HISTORY_FILE (JSON
lines written by xhisper.sh, already trimmed to history-size). Only one
window exists at a time: a second launch raises it.

Look and motion follow design A (macos/History.swift, HistoryLayout.swift),
the same numbers in logical pixels. The dictated text never goes to argv or
to the log.
"""

